# Last updated: 2026-08-29 07:25:59 (Buenos Aires) by Morgan F, to version 6
# Install as .github/workflows/personal-pack-sync.yml in a repo that
# vendors the personal pack (process/personal/, tracked by
# process/manifest_personal.json). Scheduled, unattended sibling of
# bestpractice-upstream-sync.yml: checks whether the pack's source repo,
# RepoPersonalPreferences (private — Morgan's own rulebook,
# https://github.com/themorgan/RepoPersonalPreferences), has moved past
# process/manifest_personal.json's recorded upstream.commit, and if so,
# takes the update, integrates it using its own judgment, and merges it —
# without waiting for a session to notice. See process/personal/README.md
# [`pack-sync`](process/personal/README.md#pack-sync).
#
# Unlike bestpractice-upstream-sync.yml, RepoPersonalPreferences is PRIVATE,
# so both jobs need a repository secret with read access to it:
# PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN (a GitHub personal access token — fine-grained,
# read-only, scoped to just that one repo, is enough). No workflow here can
# mint or install that secret; an administrator sets it once by hand
# (NEW_REPO_SETUP.md step 8 / GETTING_STARTED.md's administrator section).
# `check` costs one authenticated `git ls-remote` and never calls the
# model, so a quiet run costs nothing. `update` only runs when the pack
# actually moved. Every run of `check` also emits a `::warning::` GitHub
# Actions annotation if PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN isn't set — a deliberate
# per-run smoke test surfaced in the Actions UI, not just a log line, so a
# revoked or missing token is noticed the same day rather than by chance.
#
# `check` also verifies a Claude credential is configured — either
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY satisfies it, since `update`
# calls Claude Code and can't run without one. If the pack moved but
# neither secret is set, `update` is skipped (rather than attempted and
# failing on an auth error) and `note-missing-credential` leaves a clear
# `::warning::` in the run's summary instead — distinct from a missing
# PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN above, which stays a silent skip (see the SECURITY
# NOTE below: that credential is fine to skip quietly, but a missing
# Claude credential is worth flagging since it blocks every unattended
# run, not just this one). A chat session asked to run this sync manually
# doesn't need either secret at all — it can just take the update itself,
# in-session, following the same steps below — but should still remind
# the user to set one so future unattended runs don't need to be asked
# for.
#
# SECURITY NOTE: the token is passed to the "update" job's Claude Code step
# as an env var, never interpolated into the prompt text — a `${{ secrets.* }}`
# expression inside a `prompt:` string would hand the raw token to the model
# call itself, outside GitHub's own log-masking, rather than just to the
# job's shell environment. The prompt below tells the agent to read
# $PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN from its own environment instead.
#
# Model pinned to claude-sonnet-5 at effort high (see below) — the
# account this sync authenticates as (a Pro/Max subscriber's
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) would otherwise decide the
# runtime default (Sonnet 5 on Pro, Opus 5 on Max or the API), so an
# unpinned run could silently switch models depending on which secret is
# configured. Pinning keeps behavior identical either way.
#
# Frequency defaults to weekly; switching to daily is a one-line swap.
# Cron is UTC-only, so both lines below convert from Buenos Aires local
# time (America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires, UTC-3 year-round, no DST since
# 2009 — verified 2026-08-21) by adding 3 hours. This slot is deliberately
# outside Morgan's working hours — an unattended run that opens and
# merges its own PR is easier to skim as a finished thing the next
# morning than to have land mid-workday. It no longer needs to dodge
# the BestPractice sync's own slot (that one stays on Mondays, at
# Alex's — BestPractice's owner's — preferred time), but the two
# workflows still never touch the same working tree on the same day, so
# there's nothing to keep apart. To change frequency, comment out the
# active `- cron:` line and uncomment the other one; to change time of
# day, adjust either line's hour/minute the same way.
name: Personal pack sync

on:
  schedule:
    # Weekly (default): every Tuesday at 04:15 Buenos Aires.
    - cron: '15 7 * * 2'
    # Daily: uncomment this line and comment out the weekly one above.
    # - cron: '15 7 * * *'
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  check:
    name: Check pack source
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
      issues: write
    outputs:
      moved: ${{ steps.check.outputs.moved }}
      credential_set: ${{ steps.credential-check.outputs.credential_set }}
    steps:
      - name: Check out repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          # actions/checkout's default persist-credentials: true injects the
          # job's own ephemeral GITHUB_TOKEN (scoped only to THIS repo) as a
          # git http.extraheader for all of https://github.com/ -- which
          # silently overrides the x-access-token:$PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN@
          # credentials embedded in the git ls-remote URL below, since both
          # target github.com. Without this, the check below fails with
          # "Repository not found" against the pack source no matter how
          # correctly PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN itself is scoped.
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Check whether a Claude credential is set
        id: credential-check
        env:
          ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}
          CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN }}
        run: |
          if [ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] || [ -n "${CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN:-}" ]; then
            echo "credential_set=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          else
            echo "credential_set=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          fi

      - name: Compare recorded commit against the pack source's HEAD
        id: check
        env:
          PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN }}
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if [ -z "${PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN:-}" ]; then
            echo "::warning::PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN secret not set -- cannot reach the private pack source (RepoPersonalPreferences); the personal-pack sync is skipping this run. Set the PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN repository secret (see GETTING_STARTED.md's administrator section) if this is unexpected."
            python3 process/personal/tools/report_automation_issue.py \
              automation-blocked:personal-pack-sync-token \
              "Personal pack sync blocked: PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN not set" \
              "The personal-pack sync can't reach its private source (RepoPersonalPreferences) because the \`PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN\` repository secret isn't set -- every scheduled run is skipping silently until it is.

          Generate a fine-grained, read-only token scoped to just \`themorgan/RepoPersonalPreferences\` and add it at **Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret**, named \`PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN\` (see GETTING_STARTED.md's administrator section).

          Run: $GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID"
            echo "moved=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
            exit 0
          fi
          REPO=$(python3 -c "import json;print(json.load(open('process/manifest_personal.json'))['upstream']['repo'])")
          RECORDED=$(python3 -c "import json;print(json.load(open('process/manifest_personal.json'))['upstream']['commit'])")
          AUTHED=$(echo "$REPO" | sed "s#https://#https://x-access-token:${PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN}@#")
          HEAD=$(git ls-remote "$AUTHED" HEAD | cut -f1)
          echo "recorded=$RECORDED  head=$HEAD"
          if [ -n "$HEAD" ] && [ "$HEAD" != "$RECORDED" ]; then
            echo "moved=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          else
            echo "moved=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          fi

  note-missing-credential:
    name: Note skipped run (no Claude credential set)
    needs: check
    if: needs.check.outputs.moved == 'true' && needs.check.outputs.credential_set == 'false'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
      issues: write
    steps:
      - name: Check out repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Explain why this run did nothing
        run: |
          {
            echo "The personal pack's source has moved, but neither \`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\` nor \`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\` is set, so this sync could not take the update automatically this time."
            echo ""
            echo "Set one of the two secrets at **Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret** so future runs can take the update unattended (see GETTING_STARTED.md's administrator section), or ask a chat session to take this update manually in the meantime."
          } | tee -a "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
          echo "::warning::Personal pack sync skipped: neither CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN nor ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set."

      - name: Open or update a GitHub issue (process/personal/README.md [`automation-issues`](process/personal/README.md#automation-issues))
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        run: |
          python3 process/personal/tools/report_automation_issue.py \
            automation-blocked:personal-pack-sync \
            "Personal pack sync blocked: no Claude credential set" \
            "The personal pack's source has moved, but neither \`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\` nor \`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\` is set, so the scheduled sync could not take the update.

          Set one of the two secrets at **Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret** (see GETTING_STARTED.md's administrator section), or ask a chat session to take the update manually in the meantime -- it doesn't need either secret, since it's already Claude.

          Run: $GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID"

  update:
    name: Take the update, integrate, PR, merge
    needs: check
    if: needs.check.outputs.moved == 'true' && needs.check.outputs.credential_set == 'true'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: write
      pull-requests: write

    steps:
      - name: Check out repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0
          # See the same option's comment in the check job above: without
          # this, the persisted GITHUB_TOKEN credential (scoped only to this
          # repo) shadows PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN for any later git operation
          # against the pack source, which is a different repo.
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Set up Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"

      - name: Install check dependencies
        run: python -m pip install cmarkgfm pyyaml

      - name: Run Claude Code to take the update
        uses: anthropics/claude-code-action@v1
        env:
          PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN }}
        with:
          claude_code_oauth_token: ${{ secrets.CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN }}
          anthropic_api_key: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}
          claude_args: '--model claude-sonnet-5 --effort high'
          prompt: |
            The personal pack's source repo (process/manifest_personal.json
            upstream.repo — private) has moved since this repo's vendored
            copy at process/personal/ was last synced. Take the update,
            unattended:

            1. A PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN environment variable is already set in
               this job for authenticating against the private source repo
               — never echo it, never write it into a commit message, PR
               text, code, or a log line; use it only to build an
               authenticated clone URL, e.g.
               `https://x-access-token:$PERSONAL_PACK_TOKEN@github.com/OWNER/REPO.git`
               (read OWNER/REPO from process/manifest_personal.json
               upstream.repo). Clone it to a scratch directory.
            2. Compare: `python3 process/personal/tools/pack_sync.py status
               <clone>` diffs this repo's process/personal/ against the
               clone's process/personal/ subtree and shows the recorded vs.
               actual commit.
            3. Mirror the change: `python3 process/personal/tools/pack_sync.py
               update <clone>` pulls the clone's default branch, overwrites
               process/personal/ with its process/personal/ subtree, and
               records the new commit into process/manifest_personal.json's
               upstream.commit in one step — there is no landing-PR phase
               for this direction, the source repo already IS the pack's
               canonical copy (unlike BestPractice's own check-in loop).
            4. Re-weave anything that changed in
               process/personal/templates/AGENTS_ADDENDUM.md.template into
               this repo's own AGENTS.md "Personal setup rules" section by
               hand (three-way merge: old template vs new template vs this
               repo's adapted wording) — never clobber a local adaptation.
               Do the same for any other installed, adapted copy tracked in
               process/manifest_personal.json's entries (the workflow
               templates, tools/bootstrap.sh's identity lines): apply the
               template's change through whatever local adaptation that
               entry's notes describe, then re-baseline it —
               `process/upstream/tools/practice_audit.py --update-baseline`
               covers process/manifest_personal.json too, in the same run.
            5. Run the repo's gates and make sure they all pass before
               committing anything:
               python3 process/upstream/tools/doc_lint.py --all
               python3 process/personal/tools/light_check.py --all
               python3 process/upstream/tools/practice_audit.py
            6. Resolve TODO.md's own record of this drift, in the same
               commit: `python3 process/personal/tools/pack_sync.py resolve
               personal-pack "unattended sync -- see this PR"`. This update IS
               the review a session-start notice (process/personal/README.md
               [`drift-notice`](process/personal/README.md#drift-notice)) would otherwise have been asking a human to do -- if this
               unattended run got here first, TODO.md's "## Pending Drift
               Reviews" section (if it has an open `personal-pack` entry)
               would otherwise sit stale, still claiming the drift is
               unreviewed after this PR already resolved it. This command is
               a no-op (prints a note, exits 0) when there's no open entry,
               so it's always safe to run.

            Judgment calls you make while merging (a conflict between a pack
            change and a local adaptation, a template change that doesn't
            map cleanly onto this repo) are exactly what a human should skim
            before trusting an unattended merge. List every one of them,
            plainly, in the commit message body — not just the PR
            description — under a "Judgment calls to review:" heading. If
            there are none, say so explicitly rather than omitting the
            heading.

            Commit as author "Morgan F <morgan@westegg.com>" (reuse the
            address already used by prior commits in this repo's history —
            do not guess a different one). Add yourself as
            Co-Authored-By. Add a trailer `Session: <this workflow run's
            URL>` — build it from
            `$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID`
            — since there is no chat session behind an unattended run.

            Push a branch, open a pull request against the default branch
            summarizing what the pack changed and restating the judgment
            calls from the commit message, wait for this repo's own checks
            (Markdown lint, light check, practice_audit) to report success
            on the PR, then merge it. If any check fails and you cannot fix
            it confidently, leave the PR open, unmerged, with a comment
            explaining exactly what failed and why you stopped — do not
            force a merge past a failing check.
